---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { AGENTENV, CHECKLIST } from '../../data/environments';
import { pathFor } from '../../lib/site';
---
<BaseLayout
  lang="en"
  title="What is AgentEnv + REA? FAQ | rea.run"
  description="REA records authorized browser sessions; Scale AgentEnv exposes replay as MCP tools. rea.run mirrors the HF catalog."
  path="/faq/agentenv-rea/"
>
  <article class="prose-page mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-14">
    <p class="text-sm"><a class="quiet-link" href="/faq/">← FAQ hub</a></p>
    <p class="badge badge-accent mt-4">FAQ · AgentEnv</p>
    <h1 class="display mt-4 text-4xl text-[var(--color-ink)]">What is AgentEnv + REA?</h1>
    <p class="lede mt-4 !max-w-none">
      How recorded browser sessions become replay environments — and what rea.run does (and does not) provide.
    </p>

    <h2>Short answer</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>REA</strong> can record browser sessions / HAR against targets you are authorized to analyze.</li>
      <li><strong>Scale AgentEnv</strong> turns those captures into RL-style environments and exposes replay as <strong>MCP tools</strong>.</li>
      <li><strong>earakely-scale (Scale Labs)</strong> published 50+ such environments on Hugging Face.</li>
      <li><strong>rea.run</strong> mirrors that catalog for community teaching: categories, notes, baselines, deep links — not the runtime.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Suggested path</h2>
    <ol>
      {CHECKLIST.en.map((s) => <li>{s}</li>)}
    </ol>

    <h2>Where to go next</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><a href={pathFor('en', '/environments/')}>Environments mirror on rea.run</a></li>
      <li><a href={AGENTENV.collection} rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">HF collection</a></li>
      <li><a href={AGENTENV.space} rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">HF Space gallery</a></li>
      <li><a href={AGENTENV.blog} rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Introducing AgentEnv</a></li>
      <li><a href={pathFor('en', '/docs/install/')}>Install REA</a></li>
      <li><a href={pathFor('en', '/faq/agentenv-hosting/')}>Do you host the RL envs?</a></li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Authorized use only</h2>
    <p>
      Capture and replay only against software you own, OSS under a compatible license, malware in an approved lab,
      or with written permission. See <a href={pathFor('en', '/faq/legal-boundary/')}>legal boundary</a>.
    </p>

    <footer class="mt-12 border-t border-[var(--color-line)] pt-6 text-sm text-[var(--color-muted)] not-prose">
      <p class="text-xs uppercase tracking-wider">Attribution</p>
      <p class="mt-2">{AGENTENV.attribution}</p>
      <p class="mt-4"><a class="quiet-link" href={pathFor('en', '/compliance/')}>Compliance</a></p>
    </footer>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
